 rockwork was  worried for the students he then thinks  to himself that he's  acknowledged them as heroes and trusts  them to do the job correctly  during the flashback scenes that follow  this moment we get a look back to  episode one  when bakago brutally mocked deku in  front of the entire class  for being quirkless i think potentially  one of the reasons we are seeing this  flashback in particular  is because by the end of these events  that are happening bakugou himself may  be quirkless i'm not saying it's going  to happen 100  or anything but by the end of this video  you'll see what i'm thinking  the scene then flashes back even further  to a moment we've never seen before  in these panels we see a really young  deku and bakugou  watching all might on the tv as he saves  a civilian from a monster  this is the moment that i think  potentially could have been a mistake  from harukoshi  but let me know what you guys think when  we look at all my shoulders there is  clearly smoke coming from them  which of course is what usually happens  when he's at the limit  of holding his muscle form from our  understanding  all might was in good shape up until his  battle with all for one  which was five years before the first  episode of the series  it was only after that moment that his  health deteriorated  and this was best demonstrated by this  graph that we saw in the first maya  academia movie  and given the timelines here i mean look  how young deku and bakugo are this  clearly  wasn't five years ago it's clearly way  before that which means that all might  should have been perfectly healthy  we all know the connotations with all  might and smoke like harakoshi has  basically established that since day one  so i think it just may have been a  mistake but let me know  following this we get a cool combination  of the past and the present  in which bakugou looks up at deku  fighting shigaraki  and remembers his words way back in  chapter 8 in which midoriya said that he  would no longer be the punching bag deku  but instead he's the deku who always  does his best  this was a nice touch from hirokoshi and  a very cool way of signifying deku's  growth right  way back in chapter eight he was almost  in a sense he was afraid to face back a  girl like you can see it in his face  and now he's fighting shigeraki who is a  million times stronger than bagago  and deku just has no fear he doesn't  care about himself  he's thinking about saving everyone else  regardless of what happens to him  moving on though the two most  interesting aspects of this chapter  are located in its final pages number  one is the return of all for one  and number two is bakago's sacrifice to  protect deku  if you've seen my spoiler review you'll  know that endeavor grabs shiguraki and  then unleashes  his prominence burn but it's at this  moment  that afo seemingly swoops in and hijacks  tomorrow's body  from the leaks that came out on thursday  this was not clear at all  but now we get the clarification that  yeah afo is now  just in control earlier in the chapter  shiguraki was begging himself  almost to find a quirk that could deal  with deku and it seems that in this  moment  afo has answered that call it reminds me  of when your brother or sister will ask  you for help on a game  and then instead of telling them what to  do you just grab the controller and do  it yourself  that said it's unclear exactly how long  afo  is about to be in control because many  chapters ago  we saw how his spirit was trying to  control shigaraki in a sense  but shiggy was able to destroy that  vestige and  i thought that was the end of it the  fact that he was able to show shiguraki  so much compassion up until this point  that was surprising so the idea that it  was all a facade and in reality  he just wanted some he just wanted a  backup body all along  i can believe that either way this new  and improved awful one looks  absolutely hideous and whilst i don't  know what this speech bubble is meant to  say  i imagine it's similar to one of those  noises you would hear in the last of us  the official translation clarifies that  all for one says the words  little brother when targeting deku with  forced quirk activation  a similar thing happened a few chapters  ago in that afo doesn't really see one  thrall as just a quirk  but rather he sees it as the  personification  of his little brother in my opinion  there's probably more to the story of  off one and his brother than we've been  told about  because i mean as we know afo's brother  didn't even really like him to begin  with  so what's all for one's obsession with  him like why is he so desperate for them  to have a reunion  clearly there must be more to the story  the chapter ends with bakugou pushing  deku  out of the way and sacrificing himself  but now that i've had more time to think  about it  i'm even more certain that bakugou is  going to survive  the reason i say that is because the  blow that bakako took  was originally intended for deku and  naturally all for one wouldn't kill deku  until he could steal one for all first  that means by default  that this blow was not meant to be  critical it's not meant to kill someone  so for the time being at least bakago is  alive  and next chapter i just you know what  the likelihood is  that all for one is just going to let  baka go drop down to the floor  in the same way that he did for  endeavour because he doesn't really care  about them it's all about stealing one  for all  worst case scenario is that all for one  pulls back ago towards him  and steals his quirk in much the same  way he intended to do for deku  if that was to happen it would of course  mean that bakago  essentially sacrificed his quirk to save  deku which would be  incredibly poetic because as we all know  bakugou  bully deku for being quirkless for so  long so to then  lose his own quirk to save deku yeah  that's that's full circle right there  either way the fact still remains that  bakugou endeavor  and deku are now seriously injured and  it seems that next chapter  shoto might get the chance to shine  because everyone else is super exhausted  super injured super tired shoto is the  is the the latest person to join the  battlefield  so i would hope that he has enough  energy to  to put up a fight but anyway let me know  down below  what did you guys think of this chapter  and how high do you rate the chances of  bakugou losing his quirk  do be sure to subscribe as i'll be  discussing next week's chapter on the  channel as well  and until then peace out
 

